    25	**3.1 The prediction moves a lot under a conditioning rotation — every arm, every angle.** Released K = 8: EDT gap 23.8–26.3 ms, C50 gap 0.59–0.64 dB, T60 gap 3.1–3.8 % (18–22 ms absolute), log-spectrogram MAD 0.157–0.180, magnitude rel-L2 0.20–0.23, waveform rel-L2 0.82–0.88; the query-level gap intervals are narrow (about ± 5 %), the room-cluster intervals are much wider (released K = 8 EDT 45°: 26.2 ms [10.6, 43.7]). The exp_01 models shift less (control: EDT 10.1–16.4 ms, C50 0.30–0.44 dB, T60 1.5–2.5 %; cylindrical: EDT 7.8–14.3 ms, C50 0.23–0.38 dB, T60 1.2–2.3 %); the released checkpoint evaluated at K = 1 (trained at K = 8) has EDT gaps of 10.6–12.5 ms (below both K = 8 exp_01 arms at 45°, above both at the other angles) and is lowest on C50 / T60 at 45°, 90° and 270° (0.21–0.23 dB, 1.3–1.5 %) but not at 180°, where its C50 shift peaks (0.245 dB) and the cylindrical model is lower (0.235 dB, T60 1.23 % vs 1.44 %). For the K = 8 arms the shift is largest at 45° on every metric (the diagonal heading, as in exp_03) and similar at 90°, 180° and 270°.
    26	
    27	**3.2 The net accuracy change is small and, for the headline arm, mostly not distinguishable from zero — or an improvement.** Released K = 8 (query-level / room-level status): EDT Δ = −0.6 ms [−1.8, +0.6] at 45° and −0.9 [−2.0, +0.1] at 270° (denominator uncertain / uncertain), −1.6 [−2.7, −0.5] at 90° and −1.2 [−2.4, −0.06] at 180° (improvement at the query level; room level uncertain); C50 Δ = +0.033 dB [+0.006, +0.060] at 45° (defined / uncertain), −0.003, +0.008, +0.022 dB elsewhere (uncertain / uncertain); T60 Δ = +0.47 pp [+0.32, +0.62] at 45° (defined / defined), +0.26 at 90° and +0.16 at 270° (defined / uncertain), −0.24 at 180° (improvement / uncertain).
    28	
    29	**3.3 Reportable cells show shifts several times larger than the signed error change.** Reportable cells (query-level status "defined", converged, seed statuses agreeing), with the room-level status beside each:
